PRD: Personal Website & Blog
Document Version: 1.0
Date: October 27, 2023
Author: J Nakano
Status: Proposed

1. Introduction & Vision
This document outlines the requirements for building a modern, performant, and easily maintainable personal website. The primary purpose of this site is to establish a professional online presence, share a personal biography, and publish blog articles. The core philosophy is simplicity, performance, and a streamlined content creation workflow for the author, all while leveraging a free-to-host technology stack.

2. Goals & Objectives
Primary Goal: To launch a personal website with Home, About, and Blog sections.
Key Objective 1: The process of creating and publishing a new blog post must be as simple as adding a single Markdown file to the project.
Key Objective 2: The website must be extremely fast, accessible, and responsive on all common devices (mobile, tablet, desktop).
Key Objective 3: The entire project must be deployable and hostable on Netlify's free tier.
Success Metric: A new blog post can be written, committed to Git, and be live on the production URL within minutes, without any manual steps beyond git push.

3. Target Audience
Technical Peers & Community: Colleagues and other developers who may be interested in the technical content of the blog.
Potential Employers & Collaborators: Individuals looking to understand my skills, experience, and communication style.
General Readers: Individuals who discover the blog through search engines or social media, interested in the topics discussed.

4. Core Features & Functional Requirements
4.1. Global Elements
Header:
Must be present on all pages.
Must contain the site title (linking to the Home page).
Must contain a primary navigation menu.
Navigation:
Must contain links to: Home, About, Blog.
Links should clearly indicate the active page.
Footer:
Must be present on all pages.
Must contain a copyright notice with the current year and site title.

4.2. Pages & Templates
Home Page (/)
Purpose: A landing page to welcome visitors.
Content: A main headline, a brief introductory paragraph.
About Page (/about/)
Purpose: To provide a professional biography.
Content: A headline, paragraphs containing the bio text.
Blog Listing Page (/blog/)
Purpose: To display a reverse-chronological list of all published blog posts.
Functionality:
It must query Eleventy's posts collection.
Posts must be sorted with the newest first.
Each item in the list must display the post's title and its publication date.
The title must be a link to the individual post page.
Individual Blog Post Page (/blog/my-post-slug/)
Purpose: To display the full content of a single blog post.
Content:
Post Title.
Publication Date.
Full post content rendered from Markdown.
Functionality:
Must support standard Markdown syntax (headings, lists, links, etc.).
Code blocks must be syntax-highlighted.

4.3. Blog Post Workflow
Creation: A new post is created by adding a new Markdown (.md) file to the src/posts/ directory.
Front Matter: Each post must contain the following front matter:
title: (String) The title of the post.
date: (Date) The publication date (e.g., YYYY-MM-DD).
layout: (String) Path to the post layout file (e.g., "layouts/post.njk").
tags: (Array of strings) Categories for the post (e.g., ["tech", "eleventy"]).
permalink: (String, optional but recommended) To define a clean URL structure (e.g., "/blog/my-post-slug/").

5. Technical Specifications
5.1. Technology Stack
Static Site Generator: Eleventy (11ty)
Styling: Tailwind CSS (via PostCSS)
Templating Language: Nunjucks (.njk)
Content Format: Markdown (.md)
JavaScript: Vanilla JavaScript (for potential minor client-side interactions)
