5.3. Build Process & Scripts (package.json)
The following npm scripts shall be configured:
Generated json
"scripts": {
  "build:css": "tailwindcss -i ./src/assets/css/styles.css -o ./_site/css/styles.css --minify",
  "build:eleventy": "eleventy",
  "build": "npm run-all build:*",
  "start:css": "tailwindcss -i ./src/assets/css/styles.css -o ./_site/css/styles.css --watch",
  "start:eleventy": "eleventy --serve",
  "start": "npm-run-all --parallel start:*"
}
Use code with caution.
Json
npm start: For local development. Runs a local server with live-reload for both content and style changes.
npm run build: For production builds. Generates the complete, optimized site in the _site directory.
5.4. Deployment & Infrastructure
Hosting Provider: Netlify (Free Tier)
Deployment Method: Continuous Deployment via a Git repository (GitHub, GitLab, etc.). Pushing to the main branch will trigger a production build.
Build Configuration: Defined in netlify.toml:
Generated toml
# netlify.toml
[build]
  command = "npm run build"
  publish = "_site"

[context.production.environment]
  NODE_ENV = "production"
