6. Design & UX Requirements
Layout: The design must be responsive and mobile-first. Content should be legible and accessible on screen sizes from 320px width upwards.
Styling: A minimalist and clean aesthetic using Tailwind CSS utility classes. The color palette should be simple, primarily using shades of gray with a single accent color for links and highlights.
Typography: Default to system fonts for performance and a native feel. Font sizes and line heights should ensure high readability.

7. Out of Scope (Version 1.0)
Comments Section: No third-party or native comment system will be implemented.
CMS Integration: Content will be managed directly in Markdown files within the Git repository.
Search Functionality: No site-wide search will be included.
Dark Mode: A single (light) theme will be implemented.
Analytics: No analytics scripts will be included in the initial build.

8. Acceptance Criteria
A checklist to confirm project completion:
The project structure is created as defined in section 5.2.
All dependencies in package.json are installed.
npm start successfully launches a local development server on localhost:8080.
All three pages (Home, About, Blog) are accessible and render correctly on the local server.
Navigation between pages works correctly.
Creating a new .md file in src/posts/ and restarting the server results in the new post appearing on the /blog/ page.
npm run build command completes without errors and populates the _site directory.
The layout is responsive when tested on mobile and desktop viewports.
Code blocks within a blog post are correctly syntax-highlighted.
The project is successfully linked to a Netlify account and deploys automatically on git push.
The live Netlify site matches the result of the local production build.